Package: sentinel
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: AlexGromer <noreply@github.com>
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/AlexGromer/sentinel
Description: Autonomous self-healing UI-testing agent — control-plane binaries
 Sentinel explores a web application, grounds a plan against what it actually
 found, freezes it as a replayable scenario, and heals locators that drifted.
 .
 This package ships the Go CONTROL PLANE only: agentctl (CLI), control-api
 (HTTP + browser UI), store-gateway (persistence) and orchestrator. They
 are statically linked and need no further libraries.
 .
 IT DOES NOT SHIP A RUNNABLE TEST STACK. Driving a real browser run additionally
 requires, on this host: Python 3.11+ with uv (the planning/healing brain), Node
 24+ (the Playwright executor) and the Playwright browser binaries. Install those
 yourself, or use the container image
 (ghcr.io/alexgromer/sentinel) which carries the whole stack. Without them
 agentctl still works as a client against a control-api that has them.
 .
 The bundled systemd unit for control-api is installed DISABLED — nothing starts
 on install. See /usr/share/doc/sentinel/README.Debian.
